❓ ZIRCON — FAQ

Below are some common questions about ZIRCON: Dark Liquidity Intent Layer (fhEVM).

🔐 About Privacy and FHE

Q1. What is Fully Homomorphic Encryption (FHE)?
A1. FHE allows computations to be performed directly on encrypted data — without ever decrypting it. This ensures complete user privacy at the smart contract level.

Q2. Can validator nodes read user data?
A2. No. All order values (price, amount, side) are stored as ciphertexts on-chain and never revealed in plaintext.

⚙️ About ZIRCON Architecture

Q3. What is the role of the “Client / Wallet” in this system?
A3. The wallet encrypts the order before sending it to the blockchain, and only the owner’s wallet can decrypt it locally.

Q4. How does the fhEVM Smart Contract work?
A4. The contract executes homomorphic functions such as fhe_compare and fhe_select, allowing order-matching logic to function securely without exposing any raw values.

Q5. What is the purpose of the Threshold Committee?
A5. The committee performs multi-party decryption when settlement or audit processes are required — ensuring that no single entity has full control or access to user data.

🧩 Integration & Ecosystem

Q6. Can ZIRCON be integrated with other DEXs?
A6. Yes. The layer is modular and fully EVM-compatible, making it easy to integrate with existing decentralized exchanges.

Q7. Is this project open-source?
A7. Yes. It is released under the MIT License, available in the main repository (LICENSE file).

